  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia - Indonesia Partnership for Knowledge Sector Initiative</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Australia Indonesia Partnership Knowledge Sector Initiative (KSI) supports Indonesian policymakers to develop pro poor policies through better use of research, data and analysis. This initiative will enable planners and policy makers to draw on high quality data and evidence including government-led analysis and policy advice from independent policy institutes. KSI works with independent policy institutes and government agencies to strengthen the quality and policy-relevance research and how it is used for policymaking. KSI works to improve regulations and practices that support quality research and make using evidence in policymaking easier.</narrative>
  </description>
